7. PYTHON PACKAGES IMPORTED BY SRC/
===============================================================================

For every row: "Version" means read `Name`/`Version` in the named
`*.dist-info/METADATA` folder (the folder name itself carries the version),
and "Text" means the `licenses/` subfolder plus the `License:` /
`License-Expression:` / `License-File:` fields of that `METADATA`.
Usage notes name representative importing files; the import may be used more
widely across `src/`.

a) numpy
   Use: numerical arrays across video/image pipelines (e.g.
   `src/core/runtime.py`, `src/core/nr_composition.py`,
   `src/neural_rendering/video/*`, `src/upscale/video/media.py`).
   License: BSD-3-Clause plus bundled permissive texts (see METADATA
   `License-Expression` and `License-File` list).
   Text: `bin/python-*-embed-*/Lib/site-packages/numpy-*.dist-info/`.

b) PyAV (`av`, including `av.codec.hwaccel`)
   Use: media probing/decode/encode paths (e.g. `src/core/ffmpeg/probe.py`,
   `src/core/ffmpeg/nut.py`, `src/upscale/video/*`,
   `src/neural_rendering/video/*`, `src/frame_interpolation/*`,
   `src/live/pipeline.py`).
   License: PyAV's Python wrapper is BSD-3-Clause. IMPORTANT: the shipped
   `av.libs/` folder bundles compiled FFmpeg codec libraries and GPL
   encoders including x264/x265. Their licenses and source obligations
   apply to the shipped binary wheel in addition to PyAV's wrapper license.
   The wheel's BSD metadata is not a license for those bundled DLLs.
   Shipped DLLs: `bin/python-*-embed-*/Lib/site-packages/av.libs/*.dll`.
   Text: `bin/python-*-embed-*/Lib/site-packages/av-*.dist-info/`
   (plus section 2 for FFmpeg licensing context).

c) Pillow (`PIL`)
   Use: image decode/encode/preview (e.g.
   `src/neural_rendering/image/*`, `src/upscale/image/processor.py`,
   `src/core/nr_composition.py`).
   License: MIT-CMU (see METADATA `License-Expression`).
   Text: `bin/python-*-embed-*/Lib/site-packages/pillow-*.dist-info/`.

d) opencv-python-headless (`cv2`)
   Use: image/video helpers (e.g. `src/core/runtime.py`,
   `src/core/nr_composition.py`, `src/neural_rendering/video/guides.py`,
   `src/neural_rendering/image/batch.py`).
   License: wrapper MIT; OpenCV library Apache License 2.0 (see shipped
   `LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.txt`, which applies to the `cv2/` binary).
   Text: `bin/python-*-embed-*/Lib/site-packages/opencv_python_headless-*.dist-info/`.

e) rawpy (plus LibRaw)
   Use: RAW image decoding (`src/neural_rendering/image/decoder.py`).
   License: rawpy MIT, plus LibRaw GNU LGPL v2.1 (see shipped
   `LICENSE` and `LICENSE.LibRaw`).
   Text: `bin/python-*-embed-*/Lib/site-packages/rawpy-*.dist-info/licenses/`.

f) pillow-heif (plus its bundled codec/runtime DLLs)
   Use: HEIF/HEIC support (`src/neural_rendering/image/decoder.py`).
   License: pillow-heif source is BSD-3-Clause. Its bundled notice expressly
   identifies the shipped binary wheel as GPLv2 due to bundled libraries
   (see `LICENSES_bundled.txt`): libheif LGPLv3, libde265 LGPLv3, x265 GPLv2,
   and MinGW-w64 runtime files
   (libgcc/libstdc++ under GPL-3.0-with-GCC-exception; libwinpthread under
   MIT/BSD-style terms). Those terms apply to those shipped DLLs.
   Shipped DLLs (site-packages root): `libheif-*.dll`, `libde265-*.dll`,
   `libx265-*.dll`, `libgcc_s_seh-*.dll`, `libstdc++-6-*.dll`,
   `libwinpthread-*.dll`, plus `_pillow_heif.*.pyd`.
   Text: `bin/python-*-embed-*/Lib/site-packages/pillow_heif-*.dist-info/licenses/`.

g) resvg_py
   Use: SVG rasterization (`src/neural_rendering/image/decoder.py`).
   License: MIT.
   Text: `bin/python-*-embed-*/Lib/site-packages/resvg_py-*.dist-info/licenses/`.

h) tifffile
   Use: 16-bit RGBA TIFF output (`src/neural_rendering/image/encoder.py`).
   License: BSD-3-Clause.
   Text: `bin/python-*-embed-*/Lib/site-packages/tifffile-*.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE`.

Note on `pip`: the embed ships a `pip` wheel directory, but `src/` never
imports it and the app does not use it at runtime, so it is not listed as a
runtime dependency. Its notices remain in its own `pip-*.dist-info/`
folder should it ever be invoked.

